# 05. Intelligence Invariants

The following rules are architectural invariants.

### INV-01

A signal is not automatically an anomaly.

### INV-02

An anomaly is not automatically a threat.

### INV-03

A threat assessment is not automatically a diagnosis.

### INV-04

A recommendation is not an authorization.

### INV-05

Confidence is not certainty.

### INV-06

AI output must remain traceable to evidence.

### INV-07

Human authorization remains authoritative for consequential actions.

### INV-08

Missing data must never be silently interpreted as normal data.

### INV-09

Conflicting evidence must be represented explicitly.

### INV-10

AI-generated conclusions must never become untraceable system state.

